 **Runtime invariant:** No companion is published. Every page and frame is checked against the addressed durable Session.
+
+Session list metadata treats presentation.initialized as visible content before the first turn and retains an optional producer purpose label. Search first returns current user, assistant and authored-context messages, then adds distinct sessions whose log-only configuration explicitly declares searchable presentation.text. Arbitrary configuration values and shadowed messages remain excluded. Each search class has the existing bounded work budget; results share the ordinary total result limit.
+
+Prompt admission receives an optional expected historyVersion. Consumers validate it under the existing maintenance guard. An admission listener may return null for an already durably accepted request, preventing another enqueue. Client snapshots carry historySelection independently of the loaded event window and load selected history after opening.
+
+Host integrations submit user input through submitUserInput with a fresh request identity, durable attachments and consumer admission data. This entry is not a Remote method. It shares attachment admission, session/prompt-admission and enqueue with ordinary prompt. After validation, session/prompt-accepted persists acceptance before enqueue; failure prevents enqueue but cannot undo facts already saved. Retries use the same request identity and do not repeat admission.
